4. Discovery of the Safe Fighter

Field research has identified a new political archetype:

The Safe Fighter

The Safe Fighter can normally be found in one of the following environments:

* television studios;
* party conferences;
* parliamentary chambers;
* radio stations;
* professionally lit podcast studios;
* events protected by police;
* venues requiring attendees to pass through security.

Despite these unusually protected habitats, the Safe Fighter experiences almost continuous combat.

Typical statements include:

“They’re attacking me.”

“We’re fighting back.”

“They want to destroy us.”

“We will never surrender.”

Researchers initially became concerned for the subject’s immediate welfare.

Closer inspection commonly revealed a journalist asking a question.

