7. Heroism at Industrial Scale

The phrase:

“I will fight for you.”

has proved particularly effective.

Its rhetorical structure creates three objects simultaneously:

1. the threatened citizen;
2. the heroic protector;
3. somebody who must apparently be threatening the citizen.

This is extraordinarily economical.

Five words can produce an entire battlefield.

No battlefield planning application is required.

No soldiers need to be recruited.

No ammunition needs to be purchased.

The taxpayer therefore benefits from considerable savings.

