8. The Persecution Escalator

Researchers also identified a recurring escalation pattern.

Stage 1

Someone disagrees with the politician.

Stage 2

The politician is “under attack.”

Stage 3

The attacker becomes “the establishment.”

Stage 4

Scrutiny becomes “a witch hunt.”

Stage 5

Legal or institutional processes become evidence of persecution.

Stage 6

Supporters are instructed to “keep fighting.”

The process is unusual because contradictory evidence can reinforce it.

If nobody investigates the politician:

“They are ignoring us because they fear us.”

If somebody investigates:

“They are trying to silence us.”

If the politician wins:

“The people have spoken.”

If the politician loses:

“The system is against us.”

Researchers have therefore provisionally classified the model as highly resistant to weather.

