11. The Algorithm Discovers War

The Institute initially suspected that social-media algorithms had deliberately decided to destroy civilisation.

This hypothesis proved unnecessarily complicated.

Algorithms merely need to observe that humans click on angry things.

If:

anger → attention

and:

attention → engagement

and:

engagement → distribution

then the communications system gradually selects content capable of producing anger.

Nobody needs to instruct the machine:

“Please turn municipal planning reform into the Battle of Stalingrad.”

The incentives perform the work automatically.

Thus:

disagreement becomes confrontation;

confrontation becomes attack;

attack becomes war;

scrutiny becomes persecution;

compromise becomes surrender;

losing becomes betrayal.

Eventually everybody is fighting everybody while remaining largely seated.

