14. Enemy Manufacturing

Political disagreement normally requires two people to think different things.

Political warfare requires considerably more equipment.

An enemy must possess certain characteristics.

They cannot merely be mistaken.

They must be dangerous.

They cannot merely support another policy.

They must threaten your way of life.

They cannot merely defeat you electorally.

They must have stolen something.

They cannot merely compromise with you.

You must have surrendered to them.

Once this conversion occurs, ordinary democratic behaviour acquires suspicious characteristics.

Negotiation becomes treason-adjacent.

Compromise becomes cowardice.

Restraint becomes weakness.

The politician has successfully converted parliament back into something resembling tribal warfare while continuing to claim parliamentary expenses.

