18. Dana White Meets the Zebra

The Institute can now connect two apparently unrelated research subjects:

Dana White and a zebra.

White’s observation explains why people look at the fight.

The zebra explains what a real fight actually looks like.

Together they expose the political mechanism.

A genuine fight has enough inherent urgency to capture attention.

The rhetorical politician wants the attention without requiring the genuine fight.

Therefore the politician manufactures the perception of fighting.

The zebra has a lion.

The politician has a communications department.

Both attract attention.

Only one will be eaten if the messaging strategy fails.

