21. Courage Without Cosplay

Political courage remains real.

Researchers identified several examples:

telling supporters something they do not want to hear;

admitting an opponent has a point;

accepting legitimate scrutiny;

losing an election and actually leaving;

compromising when compromise benefits the country;

refusing to frighten people merely because frightened people click things;

lowering political temperature when raising it would produce personal advantage.

Unfortunately these behaviours produce very poor merchandise.

“WE CAREFULLY CONSIDERED THE OTHER SIDE’S ARGUMENT”

has consistently underperformed

“FIGHT BACK.”

The market has spoken.

